{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00056",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.09,
      "end_seconds": 4.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Well, morning. Nice to finally see you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.57,
      "end_seconds": 9.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "No trouble at all, come in. What's been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.88,
      "end_seconds": 13.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Okay, so I've been dealing with a bad cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.69,
      "end_seconds": 18.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "How long have you had it? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.07,
      "end_seconds": 20.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "About... well, two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.35,
      "end_seconds": 28.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.2,
      "end_seconds": 35.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "Cold air and lying down definitely sets it off. It's a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.91,
      "end_seconds": 38.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Has there been a tight chest too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.74,
      "end_seconds": 51.18,
      "duration_seconds": 12.44,
      "text": "Mm, um, yes. With tight chest, pretty mild, if I'm being honest. It's a couple of times a week. I've been coughing up yellow phlegm too, for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.11,
      "end_seconds": 54.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.72,
      "end_seconds": 56.49,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.98,
      "end_seconds": 74.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Any shortness of breath, night sweats or coughing up blood at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.15,
      "end_seconds": 81.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "No shortness of breath, night sweats or coughing up blood, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.51,
      "end_seconds": 84.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Have you had any chest pain or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.44,
      "end_seconds": 87.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.26,
      "end_seconds": 91.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.7,
      "end_seconds": 95.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Oh, no, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.86,
      "end_seconds": 103.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.24,
      "end_seconds": 112.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "I'm on telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day for my pressure. I take paracetamol, 500 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.24,
      "end_seconds": 115.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "So, how long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.41,
      "end_seconds": 118.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "About about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.25,
      "end_seconds": 120.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.73,
      "end_seconds": 123.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "No, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.25,
      "end_seconds": 127.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.82,
      "end_seconds": 131.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.04,
      "end_seconds": 133.97,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.44,
      "end_seconds": 137.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "No, I don't smoke and never have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.09,
      "end_seconds": 140.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.43,
      "end_seconds": 144.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Right, not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.83,
      "end_seconds": 157.23,
      "duration_seconds": 12.4,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.08,
      "end_seconds": 159.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.4,
      "end_seconds": 163.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.13,
      "end_seconds": 171.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had high blood pressure, yes. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.24,
      "end_seconds": 172.94,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.25,
      "end_seconds": 182.37,
      "duration_seconds": 8.12,
      "text": "Right, I've had asthma for about ten years now. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.07,
      "end_seconds": 188.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Yes, I can see the asthma in your file as well. Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.39,
      "end_seconds": 198.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.07,
      "end_seconds": 222.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 96 percent, pulse 92, respiratory rate 20. And temperature 38.3, blood pressure 121 over 75."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.84,
      "end_seconds": 227.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.58,
      "end_seconds": 231.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.07,
      "end_seconds": 248.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "No crackles at the bases."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.57,
      "end_seconds": 252.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.07,
      "end_seconds": 273.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "There are a few scattered wheezes on both sides."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.39,
      "end_seconds": 299.48,
      "duration_seconds": 21.09,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is a chest infection, probably viral. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.96,
      "end_seconds": 305.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.39,
      "end_seconds": 327.32,
      "duration_seconds": 18.93,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a chest infection, probably viral, and we'll know more once the a chest X-ray is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a bad cough for two weeks, and no leg swelling or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.84,
      "end_seconds": 329.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.15,
      "end_seconds": 352.29,
      "duration_seconds": 22.14,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a chest X-ray for cough. Let's use azithromycin, 500 milligrams, once a day, for three days. It's for chest infection. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Steam and warm fluids can ease the cough, and try to sleep with your head propped up. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.71,
      "end_seconds": 362.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.88,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. If you become breathless or cough up blood, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.93,
      "end_seconds": 364.63,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.11,
      "end_seconds": 373.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.82,
      "text": "Let's review you in a week. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.24,
      "end_seconds": 383.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.83,
      "text": "So, I take the azithromycin, 500 milligrams, once a day and come back in a week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.92,
      "end_seconds": 388.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.19,
      "end_seconds": 392.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}